            "result_text": "Done! The function uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to limit concurrency and handles KeyboardInterrupt gracefully:\n\n- **Concurrency control**: A semaphore ensures only `max_concurrent` tasks run at a time\n- **Graceful interrupts**: When Ctrl+C is pressed, it catches the signal and waits for all remaining tasks to complete (their cleanup code in `finally` blocks will run)\n- **Interrupt resilience**: Further Ctrl+C signals during cleanup are ignored so tasks aren't forcefully cancelled\n\nYou can test it like:\n```python\nfrom run import run_tasks\n\nasync def my_task():\n    try:\n        await asyncio.sleep(1)\n        print(\"Task completed\")\n    finally:\n        print(\"Cleaning up...\")\n\nasyncio.run(run_tasks([my_task, my_task, my_task], max_concurrent=2))\n```"
